  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a twenty-song set at The Mayan in Los Angeles on Tuesday, June 17, 2014 [1]. This specific performance is the only available recording for that date, captured as an audience tape by The Annotated Mountain Goats [1]. The show lasted approximately eighty-five minutes and represents the 199th entry in the archive’s collection for the band [2]. It followed their previous archived appearance on June 15, 2014, at Bottom of the Hill [2]. The setlist featured a mix of tracks, including “High Hawk Season,” “New Star Song,” and “Love Love Love” [1]. Notably, “New Star Song” was a bustout, appearing for the first time in 34 archived shows after a gap of 1,087 days [1]. Other songs included “Maybe Sprout Wings,” “Linda Blair Was Born Innocent,” and “Tallahassee” [1]. The band also performed “Southwestern Territory,” “Steal Smoked Fish,” and “Fall of the Star High School Running Back” [1]. Later in the set, they played “San Bernardino,” “Alpha Rats Nest,” and “You Were Cool” [1]. The performance continued with “Woke Up New,” “Up the Wolves,” and “Wild Sage” [1]. The final songs were “Jenny,” “No Children,” “Shadow Song,” “Black Molly,” and “California Song” [1]. This recording is recommended for its complete documentation of the evening’s lineup [1]. The audio quality reflects its origin as an audience recording from the venue [1]. Listeners can expect a full hour and a quarter of music from this Los Angeles date [1]. The setlist details confirm the order and selection of songs played that night [1].",
